---
---

<div>
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="hero-orb"></div>
    <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1;">Builders & Intermediaries · Monetise at the edge</span></div>
    <h1>Enforce address quality <span class="accent">at the edge nobody else owns.</span><span class="badge badge-accent" style="margin-left:10px;vertical-align:middle;">Net-new</span></h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">A payment or messaging hub sits at the network edge and sees routed traffic no single bank controls — which makes it the <b>broadest possible enforcement point</b> for structured-address quality. ioNova ARS gates and repairs every transiting <b>pacs</b> message in-flight, corridor by corridor, so every message leaves the hub compliant ahead of 15 November 2026.</p>
    <div class="hero-ctas">
      <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Get a sandbox <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" /><polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" /></svg></a>
      <a href="#implementation" class="btn btn-outline">See the implementation plan</a>
    </div>
    <div class="proof-bar">
      <div class="kpi-tile"><div class="kpi-value grad">widest</div><div class="kpi-label">reach of any audience</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-tile"><div class="kpi-value grad-b">days</div><div class="kpi-label">per corridor live</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-tile"><div class="kpi-value grad-t">100</div><div class="kpi-label">messages / batch call</div></div>
      <div class="kpi-tile"><div class="kpi-value grad">sub-50ms</div><div class="kpi-label">P95 pipeline</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section reveal">
    <div class="quote-card">
      <div class="quote-mark">&ldquo;</div>
      <div class="quote-text">We route for dozens of institutions. After November, a single unstructured address NAKs at the network and the disruption lands on us and everyone downstream. We need to enforce quality at the edge — corridor by corridor, in shadow first — without becoming the bottleneck.</div>
      <div class="quote-author">The problem, in their words</div>
      <div class="quote-role">Head of Hub Operations / Network Services</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">Capabilities</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">What You Can Do</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="g2">
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <div class="icon-box ib-teal"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0"/></svg></div>
        <div class="card-title">Gate-keep all routed files</div>
        <div class="card-body">The single enforcement point for traffic nobody else owns.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="badge badge-accent">Validate→Correct</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <div class="icon-box ib-blue"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M21 12a9 9 0 1 1-9-9"/><path d="M21 3v6h-6"/></svg></div>
        <div class="card-title">Repair & process pacs in transit</div>
        <div class="card-body">Every transiting message corrected inline, straight-through preserved.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="badge badge-accent">Process · In-Flight</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <div class="icon-box ib-cyan"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 5h18M3 12h18M3 19h18"/></svg></div>
        <div class="card-title">End-of-day batch run</div>
        <div class="card-body">Sweep up to 100 complete ISO 20022 messages in one overnight call.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="badge badge-accent">Process · batch</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <div class="icon-box ib-navy"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m16 3 4 4-4 4"/><path d="M20 7H4"/><path d="m8 21-4-4 4-4"/><path d="M4 17h16"/></svg></div>
        <div class="card-title">Render to MT</div>
        <div class="card-body">Down-render for legacy correspondents on the far side.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="badge badge-accent">Render</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="card card-accent">
        <div class="icon-box ib-teal"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 7V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h2M17 3h2a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v2M21 17v2a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-2M7 21H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-2"/><path d="M7 12h10"/></svg></div>
        <div class="card-title">Portfolio readiness scan</div>
        <div class="card-body">Inventory the whole traffic portfolio and flag what fails at cutover.</div>
        <div style="margin-top:16px;"><span class="badge badge-accent">Classify</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section reveal" id="implementation">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">Implementation Plan</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">From Sandbox to Live</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="g3" style="margin-bottom:var(--space-xl);">
      <div class="decision-box"><div class="decision-label">Span</div><div class="decision-body">Per corridor in days → portfolio over a longer window, shadow-mode first</div></div>
      <div class="decision-box"><div class="decision-label">Shape</div><div class="decision-body">Corridor-by-corridor In-Flight gate at the routing/conversion point</div></div>
      <div class="decision-box"><div class="decision-label">Tier entry</div><div class="decision-body">Enterprise / Partner</div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><div class="step-n">1</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Get started</div><div class="step-body">Sandbox live, first resolved address in ~2 days</div></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-n">2</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Build</div><div class="step-body">Register channels, test; ioNova tunes ~10,000 representative addresses in parallel</div></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-n">3</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Validate</div><div class="step-body">Production validation — channels + integrations exercised together</div></div></div>
      <div class="step"><div class="step-n">4</div><div class="step-content"><div class="step-title">Go live</div><div class="step-body">Swap test keys for live keys — no code change</div></div></div>
    </div>
    <div class="content-block" style="margin-top:var(--space-lg);"><p>Each routed flow binds to its own Channel Profile, so you enable the In-Flight gate at the routing/conversion point one corridor at a time, run it in shadow mode, then enforce — a corridor can be live in days. Your hub operations wire the gate (Volante VolPay, MuleSoft Anypoint, SWIFT Alliance, IBM MQ) while ioNova tunes on ~10,000 representative addresses from real routed traffic. A built-in circuit-breaker falls back to the existing flow, so you never block the bus.</p></div>
  </div>

  <div class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">Headline Benefits</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Why It Pays Off</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <span class="badge badge-green">the widest reach of any audience</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">every pacs leaves the hub compliant</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">corridor-by-corridor rollout live in days</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">shadow mode before enforcement</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">circuit-breaker fallback</span>
        <span class="badge badge-green">pre-built hub connectors</span>
    </div>
    <div class="alert alert-green" style="margin-top:var(--space-xl);">
      <div class="alert-icon"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 2 3 14h7l-1 8 10-12h-7z"/></svg></div>
      <div class="alert-content">
        <div class="alert-title">Where you start</div>
        <div class="alert-body">Partner or Enterprise tier, sized to routed volume.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Questions Answer Engines Ask</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Where does a payment hub enforce structured addresses?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>In-flight, at the routing or pain→pacs conversion point — the network edge that no single bank controls.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can we roll out without blocking traffic?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — corridor by corridor in shadow mode first, with a circuit-breaker that falls back to the existing flow.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How fast is in-flight correction?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Sub-50ms P95 for the full pipeline, preserving straight-through processing.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can it sweep messages in batch?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — up to 100 complete ISO 20022 messages per overnight call.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Does it support legacy correspondents?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — it down-renders structured addresses to MT lines without losing the structured record.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Which hub connectors are pre-built?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Volante VolPay, MuleSoft Anypoint, SWIFT Alliance and IBM MQ.</p></div></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="cta-section">
    <h3>Live in weeks — before 15 November 2026.</h3>
    <p>First sandbox call in minutes, first channel live in days. Early Adopter terms end 31 July 2026.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-outline" style="border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.25);color:#fff;">Get a sandbox</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-label">Explore</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Adjacent Solutions</h2>
    <div class="related-grid">
      <a href="/solutions/banks" class="related-card">
        <h4>Banks & PSPs →</h4><p>Two businesses, one engine.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/solutions/tms-erp-vendors" class="related-card">
        <h4>TMS & ERP Vendors →</h4><p>Ship compliance as a billable feature.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/solutions/compliance" class="related-card">
        <h4>Financial Crime Compliance →</h4><p>Sharper screening from structured data.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
